  "details": "\"Next up is looking into defining process priority as a launch option.\"\n-tupper\nIt is great to see that you are implementing this, as it will help people who have bad CPUs greatly.\nHowever setting it as a launch option means you cannot change it while in game.\nThis can lead to situations where other applications are basically inaccessible (like music players, discord, or even !SteamVR dashboard and overlays!). \nBeing able to set the process priority on the fly would be great for lower end system owners be able to adjust it according to their current needs.\n(like if they want to focus on only the game, set it to high, but if they want to do multitasking set it to normal) \nSetting it to above normal or high permanently could also cause issues with software like oculus link, airlink, and ALVR.",
